    "['ppp multilink', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ml-ppp unit 0 ppp-multilink', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ml-ppp unit 0 ppp-multilink\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, multilink PPP is configured under the `ml-ppp` interface type\\n2. The `unit 0` is the logical unit number (similar to Cisco's interface concept)\\n3. The `ppp-multilink` statement enables multilink PPP functionality, which is equivalent to Cisco's `ppp multilink` command\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ml-ppp unit 0 ppp-multilink'}]]": 1,
    "['ppp multilink group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ml-1 multilink-bundle-name \"1\"', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `ppp multilink group 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ml-1 multilink-bundle-name \"1\"\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you\\'re configuring under a serial interface in Juniper, it would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces se-1/0/0 multilink-bundle \"1\"\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact interface naming (se-1/0/0 vs serial1/0/0) may vary slightly depending on Juniper platform. The first version assumes configuration of the multilink interface itself, while the second shows how to assign a serial interface to the bundle.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ml-1 multilink-bundle-name \"1\"'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces se-1/0/0 multilink-bundle \"1\"', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `ppp multilink group 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ml-1 multilink-bundle-name \"1\"\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you\\'re configuring under a serial interface in Juniper, it would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces se-1/0/0 multilink-bundle \"1\"\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact interface naming (se-1/0/0 vs serial1/0/0) may vary slightly depending on Juniper platform. The first version assumes configuration of the multilink interface itself, while the second shows how to assign a serial interface to the bundle.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces se-1/0/0 multilink-bundle \"1\"'}]]": 1,
